Subject: [PATCH] media: capture device counts from the profile

The reference M4 Max enumerates one audioinput, one videoinput and one
audiooutput. Our build enumerated an audiooutput and nothing else: a MacBook
Pro with no microphone and no camera, which is not a MacBook Pro. It is a
property of the headless host, and it is readable from any page with no
permission — enumerateDevices() returns the counts before it returns anything
identifying.

The profile sets a floor, not an exact count. If the host genuinely has capture
hardware those devices are real and are kept, and only the shortfall is made
up. Removing real devices to hit an exact count would break capture on a
machine that can actually capture, to fix a number.

Counts rather than booleans because a machine can have several cameras, bounded
at 16 so that a malformed profile cannot make the browser synthesise an
unbounded device list.

This patch parses the counts. It does not emit the devices: patch 0092 does
that, at the audio manager and the video capture device factory, because those
are the two objects the rest of the browser asks both what devices exist and
open this one. An earlier version of this patch injected the devices into
MediaDevicesManager instead, which is only the first of those two questions,
and the result was a device that enumerated and then failed to open with
NotReadableError. That injection is gone; the reasoning it was based on was
right and was applied one layer too high.

Ledger: media.device-counts.
diff --git a/base/apostate/profile.cc b/base/apostate/profile.cc
index cd466fc..54ca7a3 100644
--- a/base/apostate/profile.cc
+++ b/base/apostate/profile.cc
@@ -196,6 +196,26 @@ Profile* Profile::ParseOrNull(const std::string& encoded) {
     }
   }
 
+  if (const DictValue* media = dict->FindDict("media")) {
+    // A machine can have several cameras, so these are counts rather than
+    // booleans. The ceiling is arbitrary but finite: it exists so a malformed
+    // profile cannot make the browser synthesise an unbounded device list.
+    for (const auto& [key, sink] :
+         {std::pair<const char*, std::optional<int>*>{
+              "audioinput_count", &profile->media_audioinput_count_},
+          std::pair<const char*, std::optional<int>*>{
+              "videoinput_count", &profile->media_videoinput_count_}}) {
+      if (std::optional<int> v = media->FindInt(key)) {
+        if (*v >= 0 && *v <= 16) {
+          *sink = *v;
+        } else {
+          LOG(ERROR) << "apostate: media." << key << " must be in [0, 16]; "
+                     << "ignoring";
+        }
+      }
+    }
+  }
+
   if (const DictValue* locale = dict->FindDict("locale")) {
     if (const std::string* v = locale->FindString("timezone")) {
       profile->timezone_ = *v;
diff --git a/base/apostate/profile.h b/base/apostate/profile.h
index 546eda3..6e71f86 100644
--- a/base/apostate/profile.h
+++ b/base/apostate/profile.h
@@ -169,6 +169,16 @@ class BASE_EXPORT Profile {
     return audio_hardware_buffer_frames_;
   }
 
+  // How many capture devices of each kind the claimed machine has. A laptop
+  // with neither a microphone nor a camera is not a laptop, and a headless
+  // host has neither, so these cannot be left to the host to answer.
+  std::optional<int> media_audioinput_count() const {
+    return media_audioinput_count_;
+  }
+  std::optional<int> media_videoinput_count() const {
+    return media_videoinput_count_;
+  }
+
   // IANA timezone name, e.g. "Europe/Warsaw".
   //
   // Only the zone *name* is a host fact. ICU's data is compiled into the binary
@@ -249,6 +259,8 @@ class BASE_EXPORT Profile {
   std::optional<std::string> screen_color_gamut_;
   std::optional<bool> screen_hdr_;
   std::optional<int> audio_hardware_buffer_frames_;
+  std::optional<int> media_audioinput_count_;
+  std::optional<int> media_videoinput_count_;
   std::optional<std::string> timezone_;
   std::optional<bool> prefers_dark_;
   std::optional<std::string> accept_languages_;
